# Probed first (2026-09-29-10-probe.play): today's actual daily is The
# Bloodgorged, 25-player normal, FALTERING ("healing lands for a quarter
# less"). Bloodgorged's own fester mechanic (direction.md hypothesis 1,
# 2026-09-26) is written specifically to punish a healer who never acts --
# every prior pull of this boss (paladin:holy/wander, priest:discipline/idle,
# priest:shadow/wander, druid:feral/auto, paladin:protection/wander) used a
# style with no combat behaviour of its own; this is the first melee-style
# pull of Bloodgorged on record, and the second paladin:protection reading of
# it (the first was wander). melee presses a rotation and steers into range
# rather than away from telegraphs, so this tests whether an actively-wrong
# tank fares differently than a passive one against the one boss this file's
# hypothesis 1 already narrowed around.
# class:2 = Paladin Tank (confirmed via probe screenshot: row1 col3, pink label).
